    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.hipatterns\n\n### Description\n\nAn error is thrown if a buffer is deleted before apply_highlighter_pattern callback gets called.\r\n\r\n```\r\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: .../share/nvim/lazy/mini.hipatterns/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua:1017: Invalid buffer id: 8\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_buf_get_lines'\r\n        .../share/nvim/lazy/mini.hipatterns/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua:1017: in function 'get_line'\r\n        .../share/nvim/lazy/mini.hipatterns/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua:945: in function ''\r\n        vim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\r\n```\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. create some large files that contain a match: \r\n```bash\r\nrm /tmp/bigfile1.js /tmp/bigfile2.js; for i in {0..10000}; do echo \"function test() { console.log('hello'); }\" >> /tmp/bigfile1.js; done; echo \"// TODO zzz\" >> /tmp/bigfile1.js; cp /tmp/bigfile1.js /tmp/bigfile2.js\r\n```\r\n2. add a keymap to swap between them fast:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal alter = true\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"n\", function()\r\n  if alter then\r\n    vim.cmd(\"e /tmp/bigfile1.js\")\r\n  else\r\n    vim.cmd(\"e /tmp/bigfile2.js\")\r\n  end\r\n  alter = not alter\r\n  vim.cmd(\"set bufhidden=wipe\")\r\nend)\r\n```\r\n3. spam the key\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nno error\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nyes error",
