            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI can reproduce (although the error seems to come from not the latest 'mini.hipatterns' version).\r\n\r\nThere is a [check for valid buffer](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/23669ab7abc2cd10f9a5166de07400bb34eaecda/lua/mini/hipatterns.lua#L909) which is done prior to actually adding highlights. Which in some extreme cases seem to be not enough, as later actual highlighting is done separately asynchronously for better non-blocking.\r\n\r\nAdding extra check there might be good enough, as it has quite low performance burden.",
